  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED, STILL VIOLATED, AND NOTHING HAS MOVED IN 17 DAYS. This item had zero discussion entries, so recording positive evidence rather than leaving it to look merely old. All five vocabularies are still divergent at dev 11a240f83d:\n\n    edge_types.py:299            {extends, inherits, implements}   the registry\n    cli.py:7250                  {extends, inherits, implements}   hand-rolled COPY\n    _transitive_bases.py:46      (extends, implements)             missing inherits\n    inherited_calls.py:137       (extends, implements, includes)   missing inherits\n    type_hierarchy.py:155/166    inline == literals                consults no registry\n\n'includes' is still absent from INHERITANCE_EDGE_TYPES, so both sub-cases stand: solidity's value is in the grouping and the consumer ignores it; ruby's value is not in the grouping at all.\n\nONE STALE REFERENCE FIXED IN PASSING: the description cites cli.py:6697 for the hand-rolled copy; it is now cli.py:7250. The constant is unchanged. Recording it because a line number that has drifted 550 lines reads as 'this was never checked'.\n\nThe open question the item raises -- is 'includes' a member of the inheritance family, ruled per-consumer -- is still unanswered and is still what blocks a sweep."  # d52e
